    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37129" root="كلأ" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ كَلِئَةٌ</span></b> , (S, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكْلَأْةٌ</span></b> , (K,) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُكْلِئَةٌ</span></b> , (S,) <i>A land containing,</i> (S,) or <i>abounding with,</i> (K,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلَأ</span>, or <i>herbage.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
The ↓ last is also said to signify <i>A land with the
pasture of which its camels have been satiated.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See a trad. quoted in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَضْلٌ</span>.

